            <ArticleTitle>[Transhepatic percutaneous embolisation of a post-traumatic pseudoaneurysm of hepatic artery].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>603-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Pseudoaneurysm of the hepatic artery is a rare complication of blunt abdominal trauma. We report a case of post-traumatic pseudoaneurysm diagnosed several months after the initial traumatism in a 18-year-old man who presented recurrent abdominal pain. This pseudoaneurysm was successfully treated by association of both classical endovascular treatment and transhepatic percutaneous embolization.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
